# Walkthrough: Dynamic Functional Payroll System

We have successfully migrated the **Payroll Management** module from static placeholders to a fully functional, premium, backend-integrated system. Both admin-facing and employee-facing views are fully synchronized, enabling dynamic calculations driven by real attendance and leave data.

---

## 🛠️ Architecture & Core Components

```mermaid
graph TD
    UserEntity[User Entity: basicSalary] -->|Reference| PayrollService[Payroll Service Engine]
    AttendanceDetails[Attendance Details] -->|Count Present/Late/Absent| PayrollService
    LeaveRequest[Leave Request] -->|Approved LOP Leaves| PayrollService
    PayrollService -->|Automatic Suggestion| PayrollController[Payroll REST Controller]
    PayrollController -->|Admin Actions| AdminUI[Payroll.jsx: Admin View]
    PayrollController -->|Employee Actions| EmployeeUI[EmployeeSalary.jsx: Employee View]
    EmployeeUI -->|Submit Request| PayslipRequest[Payslip Request Entity]
    PayslipRequest -->|HR Review| AdminUI
```

### 1. Database & Entities
*   **User Update:** Integrated `basicSalary` configuration inside `User.java` (default: 30,000.0) allowing individual compensation profiles.
*   **`Payroll` Entity:** Persists monthly earnings, HRA, performance bonus, LOP leaves, presence counts, tax/PF/ESI deductions, net payout, and payment status (`DRAFT`, `PENDING`, `PAID`).
*   **`PayslipRequest` Entity:** Allows employees to submit formal documents requests with customized reasons, editable status controls (`PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`), and automatic routing to administrators.

### 2. Dynamic Calculations Engine (`PayrollService.java`)
The core engine computes salaries using a prorated attendance and leave formula:
$$Daily\ Rate = \frac{Basic\ Salary}{Days\ in\ Month}$$
$$Unpaid\ Days = Absent\ Days + Approved\ LOP\ Leaves$$
$$Attendance\ Deduction = Daily\ Rate \times Unpaid\ Days$$

In addition to dynamic pro-rating, it applies standard professional components:
*   **Earnings:** House Rent Allowance (40% of Basic), Conveyance, Medical, and Special Allowances, and custom Performance Bonuses.
*   **Deductions:** PF (12% of Basic), Professional Tax (₹200 flat), ESI (3.25% of Basic), Income Tax/TDS, and Attendance-based pro-rated deductions.

